# Model routing

Do not burn expensive models on Q&A. Route by Cursor mode and whether you are changing code.

## Ask mode (read-only)

- Answer in this chat. Do not launch subagents unless a search is too large to do yourself.
- If you must use `Task`, set `model` to `composer-2.5-fast`. Never pick Opus, GPT-5.x, or other high-cost models.
- Do not switch to Plan or Agent just to answer a question.
- Prefer Grep, Read, Glob, and short replies over multi-agent exploration.

## Plan mode

- Use `gpt-5.6-luna-medium` or `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` on any `Task` you launch.
- Explore thoroughly and produce a concrete plan. Do not implement until the user asks.

## Agent mode (implement / edit)

- Use `gpt-5.6-luna-medium` or `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` for implementation, refactors, reviews, and verification.
- Default `inherit` is fine when this chat is already on a strong model.
- Do not fall back to `composer-2.5-fast` for coding, architecture, or debugging unless the user asks to save cost.

## Quick map

| Situation | Subagent `model` |
| --- | --- |
| Ask mode | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| Plan mode | `gpt-5.6-luna-medium` or `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` |
| Implementing or reviewing | `gpt-5.6-luna-medium` or `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` |

If a mode is unclear: questions → cheap; designing or writing code → capable.
